Author: D. Zack Garza <dzackgarza@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Oct 21 13:47:30 2026 +0000

    fix(semgrep): take no heavy-gate slot for the staged-file autofix
    
    The commit-tier autofix scans only the staged files, yet took the
    machine-wide slot before even checking whether any were staged, so every
    commit could queue behind another repository's test suite.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/justfiles/shared.just b/justfiles/shared.just
index d856edf..392295c 100644
--- a/justfiles/shared.just
+++ b/justfiles/shared.just
@@ -87,10 +87,11 @@ _format-structured-text:
 			npx -y prettier --write --config {{configs}}/prettier-global.json
 	fi
 
+# Commit tier: it scans only the staged files, so it takes no machine-wide heavy-gate
+# slot and a commit never queues behind another repository's suite.
 _semgrep-autofix:
 	#!/usr/bin/env bash
 	set -euo pipefail
-	source "{{artifacts}}/scripts/heavy-gate-lock.sh"
 	echo "============================="
 	echo "=== Running: semgrep auto-fix ==="
 	echo "# Applies Semgrep autofixes to the staged files; the ambient tier scans the whole tree"
